  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "612beaf4-f0d5-4dc0-8226-6fe3875ea3c1",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### Operators perform operations on values.\nMain categories include:\n1. Arithmetic\n2. Relational\n3. Logical\n4. Assignment\n5. Unary\n6. Bitwise\n7. Shift\n8. Ternary",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "612beaf4-f0d5-4dc0-8226-6fe3875ea3c1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "aeee3b85-d385-4bbb-8c24-1088fbd2b6e1",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 1. Arithmatic Operators\r\n```\r\n+\r\n-\r\n*\r\n/  \r\n%  ",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "aeee3b85-d385-4bbb-8c24-1088fbd2b6e1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "0c0628e7-2d94-4a3a-8939-c5371d256776",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 2. Relational Operators\r\nRelational operators compare values.\r\n```\r\n>\r\n<\r\n>=\r\n<=\r\n==\r\n!=\r\n",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "0c0628e7-2d94-4a3a-8939-c5371d256776"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e0bce859-ca4c-4f98-af40-eeb12b5f36f5",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 3. Logical Operators\r\nLogical operators operate on boolean expressions\r\n```\r\n&& (And)\r\n|| (or)\r\n!  (Not)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "e0bce859-ca4c-4f98-af40-eeb12b5f36f5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "8bc5a9ec-657c-4f83-a5c3-77b6e7d454cc",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 4. Assignment Operators\r\n```\r\n=\r\n+=\r\n-=\r\n*=\r\n/=\r\n%=",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "8bc5a9ec-657c-4f83-a5c3-77b6e7d454cc"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f0823602-dfce-4e31-97e4-3f618127024a",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 5. Unary Operators\r\n\r\nUnary operators operate on one operand.\r\n```\r\n+  (Numeric Promotion: It automatically converts smaller data types (byte, short, char) into an int.)\r\n-  (Sign Negation)\r\n++ (Increment Operator)\r\n-- (Decrement Operator)\r\n!  (Logical Not)\r\n~  (Bitwise Inversion)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "f0823602-dfce-4e31-97e4-3f618127024a"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3f3d860d-7174-49d5-899a-a9fa009940b7",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "short x = 10;\r\nvar result = +x; // The type of 'result' is promoted to int\r\n\r\nint a = 5;\r\nint b = -a; // b becomes -5\r\nint c = -b; // c becomes 5",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "3f3d860d-7174-49d5-899a-a9fa009940b7",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 1,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 1,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "4479860a-50a0-4189-84b2-4f87ca59d8c9",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "int a = 5;  // ++a first increase the valuse then assign\r\nint b = 5;  // b++ first assign , then increase the value\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(++a + \" \" + b++);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "4479860a-50a0-4189-84b2-4f87ca59d8c9",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 5,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 5,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "6 5\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3bf0104c-f551-49b9-a4ba-0bb0953e7fb4",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 6. Bitwise Operators\r\n\r\nBitwise operators operate on integral values at the bit level.It first convert the value into binary then perform the operation.\r\n```\r\n& (Bitwise And)\r\n| (Bitwise Or)\r\n^ (Bitwise Xor)\r\n~ (Bitwise Not)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "3bf0104c-f551-49b9-a4ba-0bb0953e7fb4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c594db0a-30de-4a84-9d99-a4431b9595ce",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 7. Shift Operators\r\nIt is a type of bitwise Operator.\r\n```\r\n<< (left shift)  [used to double the value]\r\n>> (Signed right shift) [used to half the value]\r\n>>> (Unsigned right shift)",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "c594db0a-30de-4a84-9d99-a4431b9595ce"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "9e81c871-4459-48fc-ba8d-3adad1cd3232",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// 1 means it shift by one position\r\n\r\nint a = 7 << 1;  // If we write 2, it will double the value 2 times i.e, 2^2 times\r\nint b = 7 >> 1;  // Shifts right while preserving the sign.\r\nint c = 7 >>> 1; // Shifts right while filling with zero bits.\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(a + \" \" + b + \" \" + c);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "9e81c871-4459-48fc-ba8d-3adad1cd3232",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 7,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 7,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "14 3 3\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "d36572e8-f694-4e87-a861-ff6df6b2d4fb",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 8. Ternary Operator\r\ncondition ? value1 : value2",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "d36572e8-f694-4e87-a861-ff6df6b2d4fb"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "366912f2-05f3-49a2-b7e4-ecd3bffb3375",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// Example:- \r\nint age = 20;\r\n\r\nString result =\r\n    age >= 18 ? \"Adult\" : \"Minor\";\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(result);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "366912f2-05f3-49a2-b7e4-ecd3bffb3375",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 9,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Adult\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 9
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "85119ffa-5aaf-4a39-9785-1f7b1f6085d9",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// It is equivalent to \r\n\r\nString result;\r\n\r\nif (age >= 18) {\r\n    result = \"Adult\";\r\n} else {\r\n    result = \"Minor\";\r\n}\r\n\r\nSystem.out.println(result);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "85119ffa-5aaf-4a39-9785-1f7b1f6085d9",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 10,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 10,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "Adult\r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 10
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}